WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.335
[rock music playing]

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.938
[screaming]

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.272
AINSLEY: I ran
through the straps.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.841
[metal scraping]

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.009
Bam, bam, bam, bam.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.177
[screaming]

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.146
AINSLEY: I dunno-- I
just-- for a second,

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.180
I thought I might get away.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.349
[rock music playing]

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.486
But then, out of nowhere,
all these police come.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.453
[thud]

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.922
Jumps on me and was
wrestling with me.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.791
Get off me!

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.961
[groaning] Get off me!

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.929
[yells]

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:30.930
They had me.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.136
Game over.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.739
[suspenseful music]

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.380
They led me to
a medical center.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.848
I knew I wasn't getting home.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.856
The doctor puts the
x-ray on this white light

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:00.427
that shows from my neck
all through my intestines.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.630
I was loaded up
from head to toe.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.099
And he goes, ay yi yi.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.701
Even the police
officers were shocked.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.003
And the doctor went to me--

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.571
[non-english speech]

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:14.307
--you do know if one of these
bursts, you're dead, don't you?

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.146
So they give me a lot of fluid--

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.314
laxative fluid.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.786
Then after a while,
[inaudible] do

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.189
you need to go to the toilet?

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.156
I need a toilet.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.624
No toilet.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.693
And they say, right, you've
got to go in that bucket.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.528
I said, what?

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:40.133
Five minutes late, I'm
squatting over this bucket,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.336
feeling embarrassed.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:47.140
I'm squeezing my stomach, and
it was like a machine gun--

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.741
[thudding]

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.910
--as all these pellets
come shooting out.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.279
[thudding]

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.380
Yeah, they hit that bucket.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.149
Pop, pop, pop, pop, pop, pop.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:02.856
Took three days to
get all of them out.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.457
[water running]

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.694
[bucket clanging]

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.732
Took me 12 hours to get 'em
in, but three days to come out.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.905
And finally, the doctor was
telling the police that,

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.708
yeah, he's-- he's clear.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.143
So I was expecting
some sort of trial,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.479
some sort of court hearing.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:29.382
But that wasn't-- no, it
didn't happen that way.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.451
Shackled by my feet,
and they escorted

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:34.220
me out directly to the prison.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.122
The prison was in the
middle of a shantytown.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.124
[whistling]

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.292
I didn't know what to expect.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.328
[dogs barking]

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:49.369
I'm waddling along
because of the shackles,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.838
and after walking--

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.072
it hits me.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.008
It's like, wow, it
was like a nightmare.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.242
[inmates whistling]

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.077
I've been to prison
many a times before,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.647
but this one was a whole
different ballgame.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.616
[inmates whistling]

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:10.723
UK prisons are like holiday
camps compared to [inaudible]..

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.493
I was scared, I was frightened.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.731
And then he said,
right, get in there.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.167
And you're going to sleep
on that floor there.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.870
[people chattering]

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:24.938
There's people everywhere.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.239
It was overcrowded.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:28.641
It was like, it's inhumane
living conditions.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:37.650
And then, when it's
time for lights out,

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.918
you see the lighters.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:41.354
[imitating lighter click]
All over the place, people

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.189
are smoking crack.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.925
And amongst the
flickers on the walls,

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:49.963
you can see these cockroaches
crawling all over people's

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:53.199
backs and over their faces.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.302
At that moment, everything
closed in on me.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.270
There's nowhere to go.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.538
I couldn't escape my demons.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.106
I couldn't escape the
nightmare I was in.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.308
I couldn't escape the
place where there was.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:10.383
I hated myself, because I
was now locked up abroad.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.753
I was now one of them people
that I'd seen on the TV

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.288
years and years earlier.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:18.458
I was now living that nightmare.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:22.228
[music playing]

